From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 5 Sep 2026 05:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] com.webos.service.camera2: allow outbound to
 com.webos.service.faceunlock

luneos-faced drives the front camera headlessly for face unlock, so
com.webos.service.camera2 has to be able to answer it. Without this every
call it makes - getCameraList, getInfo, open - times out, with ls-hubd
logging:

  LSHUB_NO_OUT_PERMS {"DEST_APP_ID":"com.webos.service.faceunlock",
  "SRC_APP_ID":"com.webos.service.camera2", ...}
  "com.webos.service.camera2" does not have sufficient outbound permissions
  to communicate with "com.webos.service.faceunlock"

The symptom is easy to misread as the camera stack hanging: luna-send from
a shell reaches the service fine, so it looks healthy, while every request
from the daemon blocks until its own timeout expires.

Note this repository also carries
0001-com.webos.service.camera2-Fix-outbound-permission-er.patch, which adds
com.webos.app.camera-* for the same reason, but that patch is not currently
listed in SRC_URI and so is never applied - hence the context here is the
pristine outbound list.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/files/sysbus/com.webos.service.camera2.role.json.in	2026-09-05 05:08:12.327520520 +0200
+++ b/files/sysbus/com.webos.service.camera2.role.json.in	2026-09-05 05:08:12.352504684 +0200
@@ -13,7 +13,8 @@
             "outbound": [
                 "com.webos.service.pdm",
                 "com.webos.service.appcasting",
-                "com.webos.service.audio"
+                "com.webos.service.audio",
+                "com.webos.service.faceunlock"
             ]
         },
         {
